Data Laboratory</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.nal.usda.gov/fnic/foodcomp/Data/HG72/hg72_2002.pdf"/><comment>Accessed June 10, 2006.</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Monnier</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Procaccio</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Stieglitz</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lunardi</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Malignant-hyperthermia susceptibility is associated with a mutation of the alpha 1-subunit of the human dihydropyridine-sensitive L-type voltage-dependent calcium-channel receptor in skeletal muscle</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><year>1997</year><volume>60</volume><fpage>1316</fpage><lpage>25</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9199552</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/515454</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schapira</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Griggs</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><collab>eds</collab></person-group><source>Blue Books of Practical Neurology Muscle Diseases</source><year>1999</year><volume>24</volume><publisher-name>Boston: Butterworth-Heinemann</publisher-name><fpage>135</fpage><lpage>175</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marchant</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellis</surname><given-names>FR</given-names></name><name><surname>Halsall</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hopkins</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mutation analysis of two patients with hypokalemic pe